#===============================================================================
#  ARDHANARISHVARA OS — ENGINEERING SUPPORT DOCUMENT
#  SovereignOS Storage Engine v5 — Reed-Solomon GF(2^8)
#  File: storage_engine_v5_reed_solomon.support
#===============================================================================
#  PURPOSE:
#    Engineering reference for the SovereignOS Storage Engine v5:
#      • GF(256) arithmetic (log/antilog tables)
#      • Reed-Solomon encoding (generator polynomial)
#      • Reed-Solomon decoding (syndromes, BM, Chien, Forney)
#      • distributed shard placement
#      • fault-tolerant reads + repair
#      • distributed snapshots
#
#===============================================================================
#  MODULE SUMMARY:
#
#    - [GF256 Arithmetic](ca://s?q=Explain_GF256_Arithmetic)
#    - [RS Generator Polynomial](ca://s?q=Explain_RS_Generator_Polynomial)
#    - [Syndromes](ca://s?q=Explain_RS_Syndromes)
#    - [Berlekamp-Massey](ca://s?q=Explain_Berlekamp_Massey)
#    - [Chien Search](ca://s?q=Explain_Chien_Search)
#    - [Forney Algorithm](ca://s?q=Explain_Forney_Algorithm)
#    - [Distributed Sharding](ca://s?q=Explain_Distributed_Shards)
#    - [Fault-Tolerant Reads](ca://s?q=Explain_RS_Fault_Tolerance)
#
#===============================================================================
#  FUNCTION OVERVIEW:
#
#    - create_volume(name, size_mb, nodes)
#         Creates RS(K+M) erasure-coded volume.
#
#    - write(volume_id, data)
#         Encodes data into K+M shards and distributes them.
#
#    - read(volume_id, shard_ids)
#         Reads shards and reconstructs missing ones using RS decoding.
#
#    - snapshot(volume_id)
#         Creates distributed snapshot.
#
#    - restore(snapshot_id)
#         Restores shard map from snapshot.
#
#    - engine_snapshot()
#         Returns engine state.
#
#===============================================================================
#  SHARD MAP FORMAT:
#
#    {
#      "RSVOL-XXXX": {
#          "SHR-A": "NODE-1",
#          "SHR-B": "NODE-2",
#          "SHR-C": "NODE-3",
#          ...
#      }
#    }
#
